course: dictionary
lesson: 519
title: The word assurance
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An assurance is a promise or a statement that makes someone feel sure, or less worried. «She gave me her assurance that she would come.» The clue is that she promised, and the promise makes you feel certain she will come.
explain: Assurance can also mean confidence in yourself. In a story, a calm character may speak «with assurance», which means they speak clearly and boldly, without doubting themselves. Check by swapping in a meaning: "with confidence" still makes sense.
explain: «In 1991 Ukraine had the world's third-largest stock of nuclear weapons on its soil.» Under the 1994 Budapest Memorandum, Ukraine gave them up in return for assurances, or solemn promises, from the USA, the UK and Russia that they would respect its borders. «Which Russia later broke» tells you those promises were not kept.
fact: An assurance is a promise or statement that makes someone feel sure.
fact: Assurance can also mean confidence in yourself.
fact: «Quality assurance» means checking that products are good.
fact: In the UK, assurance can mean a kind of insurance, especially «life assurance».
fact: A useful check is to swap in "promise" or "confidence" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «She gave me her assurance that she would come.» What is an assurance here? | A loud shout across a field | A list of school rules | *A promise that makes you feel sure | A kind of cake
exercise: «He spoke with assurance, and nobody in the room doubted him.» What does assurance mean here? | A bill to pay | Silence and shyness | Worry about the future | *Confidence in himself
exercise: In the UK, «life assurance» is a kind of what? | Weather | Sweets | A pet | *Insurance
test: In the Budapest Memorandum, what did Ukraine get in return for giving up its nuclear weapons? | A new capital city | A military base in Moscow | Gold coins to spend | *Assurances that its borders would be respected
test: What does «quality assurance» mean? | Being very hungry | *Checks that products are good | A kind of cake | A quiet, gloomy kind of sadness
exam: The speaker answered the question «with assurance» and never hesitated. What does assurance mean here? | A kind of insurance | Shyness | A promise to someone | *Confidence in herself
